   {
    "h": null,
    "level": 1,
    "paras": [
     "Apographon is a monotypic genus of snake in the subfamily Dipsadinae of the family Colubridae. The genus contains the sole species Apographon orestes, which is native to central and southern South America."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Geographic distribution",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "Apographon orestes is found in Argentina and Bolivia."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitats of Apographon orestes are forest, shrubland, and grassland, at elevations of 1,300–3,400 m (4,300–11,200 ft), and it has also been found in disturbed areas such as roadsides and pastures."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Reproduction",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "Apographon orestes is ovoviviparous."
    ]
